---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About | Ride The Tiger">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-3xl py-20">
    <header class="mb-16 border-b-4 border-tiger-500 pb-8 inline-block">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4 font-sans uppercase">About Ride The Tiger</h1>
      <p class="text-2xl text-gray-500 font-serif italic">Unvarnished peer reality for the AI creative transition.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose prose-lg prose-neutral max-w-none">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">What is Ride The Tiger?</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        <em>Ride The Tiger</em> is an independent interview publication documenting how artificial intelligence is reshaping the creative landscape. Through long-form, peer-to-peer dialogues with agency directors, independent copywriters, art directors, and creative strategists, we capture the ground truth of working with—and against—emerging generative tools.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        The name comes from the ancient paradox: <em>once you are on the tiger’s back, you cannot simply jump off without getting mauled.</em> AI isn’t going away, but blindly worshipping it is equally foolish. You have to learn to steer it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">Who It’s For</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4">
        <li><strong>Freelance Creatives & Solo Operators:</strong> Looking for pragmatic workflows and pricing strategies that keep them indispensable.</li>
        <li><strong>Agency Leaders & Design Directors:</strong> Deciding how to integrate automated pipelines without losing house style, creative prestige, or team morale.</li>
        <li><strong>In-House Marketers & Brand Strategists:</strong> Looking past Silicon Valley hype to see how real practitioners make creative work perform.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">Why You Should Read It</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4 mb-12">
        <li><strong>No Generic Prompts:</strong> We don't publish "Top 10 Midjourney Hacks" or regurgitated PR fluff.</li>
        <li><strong>Uncensored Honesty:</strong> Our guests share real client reactions, billable drop-offs, internal anxieties, and workflow secrets.</li>
        <li><strong>Balanced Candor:</strong> We celebrate genuine breakthroughs while calling out soulless slop.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="not-prose mt-12">
        <a href="/interviews" class="inline-block bg-tiger-500 hover:bg-tiger-600 text-[var(--color-charcoal)] font-bold px-10 py-5 uppercase tracking-wider transition-colors shadow-lg">Read the Interviews</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
